# mods.load — the game module list, read by nd_mods_load() at boot.
#
# One module per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are skipped.
#
# A line is one of three things
#   - a bare name WITH a module in this tree, loaded as `mods/<n>/<n>`, or
#   - a bare name WITHOUT one, which names an INSTALLED library by soname --
#     xy_load() appends the suffix and dlopen() resolves it through the normal
#     search path, so installing the package is all that is needed,
#   - a path (anything containing a `/`), taken VERBATIM -- which is how a
#     sibling module checkout is named without being copied into this tree
#     (MODS.md §4: one repo per module, ~/axil-nd-<name>).
#
# Makefile's `mods:` target applies the identical test for the first two, so
# build and load never disagree about what a bare name means.
#
# Name the STEM, not the file: xy_load() appends `.so` itself, so a line
# `level.so` makes the engine look for `level.so.so` and fail. A sibling
# module therefore appears as `../axil-nd-level/level`.
#
# Lines that name a module which is not built are reported on stderr
# ("nd_mods_load: module ... failed to load"); the engine still boots.
demo
# out-of-tree sibling repos (MODS.md §4/§0.4) and installed modules.
# Phase 1 vertical slice (MODS.md §6). `nd-core` is an installed library now:
# it has no module in this tree, so the bare name is its soname and dlopen()
# finds libnd-core.so through the normal search path. The rest are dev-tree
# checkouts named by path; Makefile's slash-module rule derives the stem with
# $(notdir $(basename $@)), so ~/axil-nd-<name>/<name> builds <name>.so.
libnd-core
../axil-nd-other/other
../axil-nd-level/level
../axil-nd-vanilla/vanilla
# Phase 2 Wave 1 (MODS.md §7). nd-shop is loaded AFTER nd-core because it
# registers an icon decorator with it: nd-core is the sole owner of on_icon and
# walks its decorator table in registration order, so a decorator loaded first
# would have nowhere to register. shop's own xy_install also xy_load()s nd-core
# by the same soname, which is a no-op refcount bump: module_load_path()
# realpath()s, so both spellings collapse to one entry.
../axil-nd-shop/shop
